nt: the expected number of steps of the random walk (edge weights as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transition rates, a loop taken with probability 2w\/d(v)) from a vertex to a target drawn"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the stationary distribution, which does not depend on the start; Σ_{i≥2} 1\/μᵢ over the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"normalized Laplacian spectrum. nil when the graph is not connected, 0 for zero or one vertex."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kemenyConstant","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":"? ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryInteger","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sz","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vol · (Σᵢ πᵢ (L_g⁻¹)ᵢᵢ − πᵀ L_g⁻¹ π), π the stationary distribution, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1\/2vol) Σᵢⱼ dᵢ dⱼ R(i, j) (commute times are vol · R), with L_g the Laplacian grounded at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the vertex of largest degree and eliminated as for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"numberOfSpanningTrees"},{"type":"text","text":". Every term is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sum of positive ones and the difference loses at most a factor n, so the result keeps its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative accuracy under any weight spread. O(n³) time, n² "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"0 is no edge.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every weight is finite and nonnegative.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Precondition"}]}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","text":"Collection"}],"title":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","abstract":[],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph/kemenyConstant(weight:)-8j44l":{"abstract":[{"text":"The Kemeny constant: the expected number of steps of the random walk (edge weights as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"transition rates, a loop taken with probability 2w\/d(v)) from a vertex to a target drawn","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the sta